{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      Nullable companyId in agents table\n      Allow agents.companyId to be nullable. ECC agents have no company. Auto-seeded on first ECC spawn if missing. Status driven by polling workflow_runs for ecc_conversation type.\n      \n        ProsReuses existing agents infrastructure (budget, heartbeat, status)No new table or migration beyond one column changeAgents page can list ECC agents naturally\n        ConsSchema change affects all code that assumes companyId not nullNeeds care to exclude from company-scoped agent queries\n      \n      ✅ Recommended — minimal schema impact, maximum reuse","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1778331120326}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      New ecc_agents table (lightweight)\n      Dedicated table: id, name, role (operator|client), status, lastActiveAt, currentTopicId. Fully decoupled from company agent model. Seeded once, status updated by orchestrator.\n      \n        ProsZero impact on existing agents infrastructureSchema exactly matches ECC needs — no nulls, no unused columnsOrchestrator updates status directly (no inference from workflow_runs)\n        ConsNew table + migration + new service + new API routeECC agents isolated — can't reuse agent budget/heartbeat machinery","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1778331120648}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      Virtual agents — no DB, derived from ECC state\n      No new rows. Agent status is computed: if workflow_runs has an active ecc_conversation run → processing. Otherwise idle. A new API endpoint GET /ecc/agents returns the two virtual agents derived from live data.\n      \n        ProsZero schema changesAlways accurate — no sync issues between agent record and actual state\n        ConsNo persistent \"last active\" or \"current topic\" — only live stateCan't store agent config/metadata (e.g. description, icon)Feels hacky — agents aren't real entities","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1778331120966}
